module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Perfect.BottomRankBettiOpen
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.FittingGeneratorOpen.Descent
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.FittingIdeals.SingularLocus
import all StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.FittingIdeals.SingularLocus

/-!
# The bottom derived-fibre Betti number of a module placed in one degree

Let `X` be a scheme, `F` a finite type quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module, `a` an integer and `s` a
natural number, and suppose the object `F[-a]` of `D(𝒪_X)` is pseudo-coherent, so that its
derived-fibre Betti function `β_a` is defined. Then

`β_a(x) ≤ s` if and only if `F` is generated by `s` sections near `x`.

This is the identification that [stacks 0BDL] uses silently when it specialises its hypothesis
`β_a ≤ r` to a module: `β_a(x)` is the dimension of the fibre `F ⊗ κ(x)`, and by Nakayama's
lemma a finite type module needs at most `s` generators near `x` exactly when that dimension is
at most `s`. With it, the closedness assertion of part (4) of [stacks 0BDL] — for `E` a module
placed in degree `a` — is available with the tag's own hypothesis, rather than with the number of
local generators standing in for it, which is how
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Perfect/BottomRankStratum.lean` states it.

The level sets of `β_a` are also treated, for an arbitrary pseudo-coherent `E`: the locus
`β_a ≥ r` is closed, because its complement is the open locus `β_a ≤ r - 1` of
`AlgebraicGeometry.BottomRankStratum.bettiLeOpen`, and hence the locus `β_a = r` is closed as
soon as `β_a ≤ r` everywhere. That is the step with which the proof of [stacks 0BDL] continues
after its first reduction: having replaced `X` by the open subscheme where `β_a ≤ r`, the
underlying set of the stratum `Z` is closed. Like the first reduction it is not a part of the
statement of [stacks 0BDL], and nothing about it carries that tag.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.BottomRankStratum.derivedFiberBetti_single_eq`: for a module placed in
  degree `a` the `a`-th derived-fibre Betti number at `x` is the dimension over `κ(x)` of the
  fibre of the module at `x`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BottomRankStratum.isGeneratedByNear_iff_derivedFiberBetti_le`: for a finite
  type quasi-coherent module placed in degree `a`, the bound `β_a ≤ s` is generation by `s`
  sections near the point.
* `BottomRankStratum.isClosedImmersion_fittingRankStratum_of_derivedFiberBetti_le`: the closedness
  assertion of part (4) of [stacks 0BDL], for `E` a module placed in degree `a`, under the tag's
  own hypothesis `β_a ≤ s`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BottomRankStratum.isClosed_le_derivedFiberBetti` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.BottomRankStratum.isClosed_derivedFiberBetti_eq_of_le`: the locus
  `β_a ≥ r` is closed, and so is the locus `β_a = r` when `β_a ≤ r` everywhere.

## Implementation notes

The fibre of `F` at `x` is read as the pullback of `F` along the canonical morphism
`i_x : Spec κ(x) ⟶ X`, and `β_a` is by definition the dimension of the degree-`a` cohomology of
the derived pullback of `F[-a]` along the same morphism; the two are identified by
`AlgebraicGeometry.BottomRankStratum.pullbackHomologySingleIso`, whose image under the global
sections functor on `Spec κ(x)` is a linear equivalence and so preserves dimension.

Nakayama's lemma enters as
`AlgebraicGeometry.isGeneratedByNear_specField_iff_finrank_le`: over the spectrum of a field
generation by `s` sections is the rank bound `s`. It is applied to the fibre, and transported to
`X` by `AlgebraicGeometry.isGeneratedByNear_pullback_iff`, which says that generation by `s`
sections near a point is insensitive to pullback — a statement about Fitting ideal sheaves
([stacks 0C3F] and [stacks 0C3D]) and not about the particular morphism `i_x`.

The spectrum of a field is a one-point space, so the point at which the fibre is tested is
immaterial; it is produced by `Nonempty` and identified with the closed point by
`Subsingleton.elim` rather than written down.

`HasDerivedCategory.standard` is installed as a local instance at high priority. At the default
priority the global `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.hasDerivedCategory` wins and silently puts
the derived pullback at the locally small model, where it says nothing about
`AlgebraicGeometry.DerivedFibreBetti.derivedFiberBetti`.

## References

* [The Stacks Project, Lemma 36.31.4 (0BDL)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BDL)
* [The Stacks Project, Lemma 36.31.1 (0BDI)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BDI)
* [The Stacks Project, Lemma 29.47.4 (05P8)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05P8)
* [The Stacks Project, Lemma 36.9.2 (0C3F)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C3F)
* [The Stacks Project, Lemma 36.9.1 (0C3D)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C3D)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry

universe u

attribute [local instance 10000] HasDerivedCategory.standard

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.BottomRankStratum

variable {X : Scheme.{u}}

/-! ### The Betti number of a module placed in one degree -/

/-- **For a module placed in degree `a`, `β_a` is the fibre dimension.** The value of the `a`-th
derived-fibre Betti function of `F[-a]` at `x` is the dimension over `κ(x)` of the module of
global sections of the pullback of `F` to `Spec κ(x)`.

The degree-`a` cohomology of the derived pullback of `F[-a]` is the ordinary pullback of `F`, by
`pullbackHomologySingleIso`; global sections on `Spec κ(x)` turn that isomorphism into a linear
equivalence, which preserves dimension. -/
public theorem derivedFiberBetti_single_eq (F : X.Modules) (a : ℤ)
    (hE : RingedSpace.IsPseudoCoherent.{u, u + 1} (X := X.toRingedSpace)
      ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor X.Modules a).obj F)) (x : X) :
    DerivedFibreBetti.derivedFiberBetti X ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor X.Modules a).obj F)
        hE a x =
      Module.finrank (X.residueField x)
        ((moduleSpecΓFunctor (R := X.residueField x)).obj
          ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (X.fromSpecResidueField x)).obj F)) :=
  ((moduleSpecΓFunctor (R := X.residueField x)).mapIso
    (pullbackHomologySingleIso F a (X.fromSpecResidueField x))).toLinearEquiv.finrank_eq

/-- **For a finite type quasi-coherent module placed in degree `a`, the bound `β_a ≤ s` is
generation by `s` sections.** A finite type quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module `F` is generated by `s`
sections near `x` if and only if the `a`-th derived-fibre Betti number of `F[-a]` at `x` is at
most `s`.

This is the identification by which the hypothesis `β_a ≤ r` of part (4) of [stacks 0BDL] reads,
for an `E` which is a module placed in degree `a`, as a bound on the number of local generators.
It is Nakayama's lemma: `β_a(x)` is the dimension of the fibre `F ⊗ κ(x)`
(`derivedFiberBetti_single_eq`), over the spectrum of a field generation by `s` sections is that
rank bound (`AlgebraicGeometry.isGeneratedByNear_specField_iff_finrank_le`), and generation by
`s` sections near a point is insensitive to pullback
(`AlgebraicGeometry.isGeneratedByNear_pullback_iff`), here along `Spec κ(x) ⟶ X`. -/
public theorem isGeneratedByNear_iff_derivedFiberBetti_le (F : X.Modules) [F.IsFiniteType]
    [F.IsQuasicoherent] (a : ℤ)
    (hE : RingedSpace.IsPseudoCoherent.{u, u + 1} (X := X.toRingedSpace)
      ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor X.Modules a).obj F)) (s : ℕ) (x : X) :
    IsGeneratedByNear F s x ↔
      DerivedFibreBetti.derivedFiberBetti X ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor X.Modules a).obj F)
        hE a x ≤ s := by
  obtain ⟨t⟩ : Nonempty ↑(Spec (X.residueField x)) := inferInstance
  have hfin : ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (X.fromSpecResidueField x)).obj F).IsFiniteType :=
    SheafOfModules.pullback_isFiniteType (X.fromSpecResidueField x).toLRSHom.toShHom F
  have hqc : ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (X.fromSpecResidueField x)).obj F).IsQuasicoherent :=
    @SheafOfModules.modulePullback_isQuasicoherent _ X.toRingedSpace
      (X.fromSpecResidueField x).toLRSHom.toShHom F ‹F.IsQuasicoherent›
  have hspec :
      IsGeneratedByNear ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (X.fromSpecResidueField x)).obj F) s t ↔
        Module.finrank (X.residueField x)
          ((moduleSpecΓFunctor (R := X.residueField x)).obj
            ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (X.fromSpecResidueField x)).obj F)) ≤ s := by
    rw [show t = IsLocalRing.closedPoint (ToType (X.residueField x)) from Subsingleton.elim _ _]
    exact AlgebraicGeometry.isGeneratedByNear_specField_iff_finrank_le
      (K := ToType (X.residueField x))
      ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (X.fromSpecResidueField x)).obj F) s
  have hpull := isGeneratedByNear_pullback_iff (X.fromSpecResidueField x) F s t
  rw [Scheme.fromSpecResidueField_apply] at hpull
  rw [derivedFiberBetti_single_eq F a hE x]
  exact hpull.symm.trans hspec

/-- **The rank `s` Fitting stratum is a closed subscheme when `β_a ≤ s` everywhere.** This is the
closedness assertion of part (4) of [stacks 0BDL] for an `E` which is a module `F` placed in
degree `a`, with the tag's own hypothesis: the `a`-th derived-fibre Betti function of `F[-a]` is
at most `s` at every point.

The hypothesis is the bound on the number of local generators of
`isClosedImmersion_fittingRankStratum_of_isGeneratedByNear`, by
`isGeneratedByNear_iff_derivedFiberBetti_le`.

The pseudo-coherence of `F[-a]` is only what the derived-fibre Betti function needs in order to
be defined; it is weaker than the perfectness the tag assumes of `E`, and nothing in the proof
uses it. -/
public theorem isClosedImmersion_fittingRankStratum_of_derivedFiberBetti_le (F : X.Modules)
    [F.IsFiniteType] [F.IsQuasicoherent] (a : ℤ)
    (hE : RingedSpace.IsPseudoCoherent.{u, u + 1} (X := X.toRingedSpace)
      ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor X.Modules a).obj F)) (s : ℕ)
    (hβ : ∀ x : X, DerivedFibreBetti.derivedFiberBetti X
      ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor X.Modules a).obj F) hE a x ≤ s) :
    IsClosedImmersion (fittingRankStratum F s).hom :=
  isClosedImmersion_fittingRankStratum_of_isGeneratedByNear F s fun x =>
    (isGeneratedByNear_iff_derivedFiberBetti_le F a hE s x).2 (hβ x)

/-! ### The level sets of the Betti function -/

/-- **The locus where `β_a` is at least `r` is closed.** Its complement is the locus where `β_a`
is at most `r - 1`, which is open because `β_a` is upper semi-continuous (part (2) of
[stacks 0BDI]). -/
public theorem isClosed_le_derivedFiberBetti (E : DerivedCategory X.Modules)
    (hE : RingedSpace.IsPseudoCoherent.{u, u + 1} (X := X.toRingedSpace) E) (a : ℤ) (r : ℕ) :
    IsClosed {x : X | r ≤ DerivedFibreBetti.derivedFiberBetti X E hE a x} := by
  have hset : {x : X | r ≤ DerivedFibreBetti.derivedFiberBetti X E hE a x}ᶜ =
      DerivedFibreBetti.derivedFiberBetti X E hE a ⁻¹' Set.Iio r := by
    ext x
    simp only [Set.mem_compl_iff, Set.mem_ofPred_eq, Set.mem_preimage, Set.mem_Iio, not_le]
  rw [← isOpen_compl_iff, hset]
  exact (DerivedFibreBetti.upperSemicontinuous_derivedFiberBetti X E hE a).isOpen_preimage r

/-- **The locus where `β_a` equals `r` is closed when `β_a ≤ r` everywhere.** Under that bound it
is the locus where `β_a` is at least `r`, which is closed.

This is the step with which the proof of [stacks 0BDL] continues after its first reduction: the
underlying set of the stratum is closed in the open subscheme where `β_a ≤ r`. It is not a part
of the statement of that tag. -/
public theorem isClosed_derivedFiberBetti_eq_of_le (E : DerivedCategory X.Modules)
    (hE : RingedSpace.IsPseudoCoherent.{u, u + 1} (X := X.toRingedSpace) E) (a : ℤ) (r : ℕ)
    (hle : ∀ x : X, DerivedFibreBetti.derivedFiberBetti X E hE a x ≤ r) :
    IsClosed {x : X | DerivedFibreBetti.derivedFiberBetti X E hE a x = r} := by
  have hset : {x : X | DerivedFibreBetti.derivedFiberBetti X E hE a x = r} =
      {x : X | r ≤ DerivedFibreBetti.derivedFiberBetti X E hE a x} := by
    ext x
    exact ⟨fun h => h.ge, fun h => le_antisymm (hle x) h⟩
  rw [hset]
  exact isClosed_le_derivedFiberBetti E hE a r

end AlgebraicGeometry.BottomRankStratum

end
